From: Andrei Kholodnyi <andrei.kholodnyi@windriver.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fast-DDS VxWorks: make shared-memory transport work across RTPs

The SHM transport did not deliver data between two RTPs on VxWorks. None of the
three causes is a VxWorks defect: each is a Fast-DDS (or vendored-boost)
assumption that does not hold on VxWorks. The fixes adapt Fast-DDS to the
documented VxWorks behaviour and are all guarded by __VXWORKS__.

1. boost::interprocess assumes _POSIX_SEMAPHORES implies cross-process unnamed
   semaphores. On VxWorks unnamed semaphores are by design not accessible from
   other RTPs (man sem_init(2rtp)): the sem_t holds only a process-local handle.
   Tell boost to use its portable spin semaphore (shared-memory atomics), which
   works cross-RTP. This is a wrong platform assumption in boost, not a VxWorks
   bug.
2. RobustExclusiveLock/RobustSharedLock assume BSD flock() semantics (the lock
   is tied to the open file and survives stat()). On VxWorks flock() is emulated
   (libunixextra) with fcntl() record locks, whose standard POSIX semantics drop
   the lock on ANY close() of the file. The stat(path) "file deleted" check opens
   and closes a descriptor internally and so releases the port owner's lock; the
   peer then judged a live port a zombie and removed it. Use fstat(fd)/st_nlink
   (which does not drop the lock) instead of stat(path), and open the _sl lock
   files O_RDWR (fcntl F_WRLCK needs a writable fd; it fails EBADF on O_RDONLY).
   The lock-dropping is correct record-lock behaviour; the mismatch is Fast-DDS
   relying on BSD flock() semantics that do not hold under fcntl emulation.
3. Fast-DDS selects thread_impl_basic (std::thread) on VxWorks, and std::thread
   silently ignores the ThreadSettings::stack_size the library intends to pass.
   Every Fast-DDS thread then got VxWorks' documented 20480 byte POSIX default
   thread stack, which the discovery thread overflows. 20 KiB is a normal
   VxWorks default, not a bug; the gap is Fast-DDS' VxWorks-unaware thread
   selection. Use the pthread implementation on VxWorks (which honours
   stack_size) and default to 512 KiB when no size is requested.
---
diff --git a/src/cpp/utils/SystemInfo.cpp b/src/cpp/utils/SystemInfo.cpp
index b44d015..d13813b 100644
--- a/src/cpp/utils/SystemInfo.cpp
+++ b/src/cpp/utils/SystemInfo.cpp
@@ -354,6 +354,20 @@ std::mutex SystemInfo::interfaces_mtx_;
 #elif defined(_POSIX_SOURCE) || defined(__QNXNTO__) || defined(__ANDROID__)
 #include "threading/threading_pthread.ipp"
 #include "thread_impl/thread_impl_pthread.ipp"
+#elif defined(__VXWORKS__)
+// VxWorks needs the pthread thread-creation path: std::thread (thread_impl_basic) ignores
+// ThreadSettings::stack_size, so threads would get VxWorks' 20480-byte POSIX default stack and overflow.
+// thread_impl_pthread.ipp honours stack_size via pthread_attr_setstacksize.
+//
+// It must be paired with threading_empty.ipp (no-op thread naming / scheduler stubs), NOT the Linux
+// threading_pthread.ipp used by the _POSIX_SOURCE branch above: that file is glibc/Linux-shaped and does not
+// compile on this VxWorks SDK -- it #includes <sys/sysinfo.h> (absent from the sysroot, guarded only by
+// !__QNX__) and references the Linux scheduler constants SCHED_BATCH/SCHED_IDLE (also absent). The only cost
+// of the empty stubs is that Fast-DDS threads are left unnamed and ThreadSettings scheduler class/priority are
+// not applied on VxWorks (cosmetic/tuning, not correctness). A dedicated threading_vxworks.ipp could restore
+// those later using pthread_setname_np (which the SDK does provide) and the VxWorks scheduler API.
+#include "threading/threading_empty.ipp"
+#include "thread_impl/thread_impl_pthread.ipp"
 #else
 #include "threading/threading_empty.ipp"
 #endif // Platform selection
diff --git a/src/cpp/utils/shared_memory/RobustExclusiveLock.hpp b/src/cpp/utils/shared_memory/RobustExclusiveLock.hpp
index 0561210..ec3aee9 100644
--- a/src/cpp/utils/shared_memory/RobustExclusiveLock.hpp
+++ b/src/cpp/utils/shared_memory/RobustExclusiveLock.hpp
@@ -248,7 +248,15 @@ private:
             // Check if file was deleted by clean up script between open and lock
             // if yes, repeat file creation
             struct stat buffer = {};
+#ifdef __VXWORKS__
+            // VxWorks: flock() is emulated with fcntl() record locks, which the kernel drops as soon as the
+            // process closes ANY descriptor of the file. stat()/lstat()/access() on a path open and close such
+            // a descriptor internally, so they must not be used while holding the lock. Use fstat() on the
+            // locked descriptor instead: st_nlink == 0 means the file was unlinked after open().
+            if (fstat(fd, &buffer) == 0 && buffer.st_nlink == 0)
+#else
             if (stat(file_path.c_str(), &buffer) != 0 && errno == ENOENT)
+#endif // ifdef __VXWORKS__
             {
                 close(fd);
                 fd = -1;
diff --git a/src/cpp/utils/shared_memory/RobustSharedLock.hpp b/src/cpp/utils/shared_memory/RobustSharedLock.hpp
index 428ee32..433a4fa 100644
--- a/src/cpp/utils/shared_memory/RobustSharedLock.hpp
+++ b/src/cpp/utils/shared_memory/RobustSharedLock.hpp
@@ -346,6 +346,13 @@ private:
 
 #else
 
+#ifdef __VXWORKS__
+    // VxWorks: flock(LOCK_EX) is emulated with fcntl(F_WRLCK), which fails with EBADF on a read-only descriptor.
+    static constexpr int LOCK_FILE_OPEN_MODE = O_RDWR;
+#else
+    static constexpr int LOCK_FILE_OPEN_MODE = O_RDONLY;
+#endif // ifdef __VXWORKS__
+
     int open_and_lock_file(
             const std::string& file_path,
             bool* was_lock_created,
@@ -354,7 +361,7 @@ private:
         int fd = -1;
         do
         {
-            fd = open(file_path.c_str(), O_RDONLY, 0);
+            fd = open(file_path.c_str(), LOCK_FILE_OPEN_MODE, 0);
 
             if (fd != -1)
             {
@@ -363,7 +370,7 @@ private:
             else
             {
                 *was_lock_created = true;
-                fd = open(file_path.c_str(), O_CREAT | O_RDONLY, 0666);
+                fd = open(file_path.c_str(), O_CREAT | LOCK_FILE_OPEN_MODE, 0666);
             }
 
             if (was_lock_released != nullptr)
@@ -374,7 +381,12 @@ private:
                     // Check if file was deleted by clean up script between open and lock
                     // if yes, repeat file creation
                     struct stat buffer = {};
+#ifdef __VXWORKS__
+                    // See RobustExclusiveLock: stat() on a path drops the fcntl()-based flock on VxWorks.
+                    if (fstat(fd, &buffer) == 0 && buffer.st_nlink == 0)
+#else
                     if (stat(file_path.c_str(), &buffer) != 0 && errno == ENOENT)
+#endif // ifdef __VXWORKS__
                     {
                         close(fd);
                         fd = -1;
@@ -418,7 +430,7 @@ private:
     {
         LockStatus lock_status;
 
-        auto fd = open(file_path.c_str(), O_RDONLY, 0);
+        auto fd = open(file_path.c_str(), LOCK_FILE_OPEN_MODE, 0);
 
         if (fd != -1)
         {
diff --git a/src/cpp/utils/thread.hpp b/src/cpp/utils/thread.hpp
index 8c07933..97124ee 100644
--- a/src/cpp/utils/thread.hpp
+++ b/src/cpp/utils/thread.hpp
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 #define UTILS__THREAD_HPP_
 
 // thread.hpp declarations
-#if defined(_WIN32) || defined(__APPLE__) || defined(_POSIX_SOURCE) || defined(__QNXNTO__) || defined(__ANDROID__)
+#if defined(_WIN32) || defined(__APPLE__) || defined(_POSIX_SOURCE) || defined(__QNXNTO__) || defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(__VXWORKS__)
 #include "thread_impl/thread_impl_custom.hpp"
 #else
 #include "thread_impl/thread_impl_basic.hpp"
diff --git a/src/cpp/utils/thread_impl/thread_impl_pthread.ipp b/src/cpp/utils/thread_impl/thread_impl_pthread.ipp
index 0c9149b..c7624fc 100644
--- a/src/cpp/utils/thread_impl/thread_impl_pthread.ipp
+++ b/src/cpp/utils/thread_impl/thread_impl_pthread.ipp
@@ -43,6 +43,18 @@ thread::native_handle_type thread::start_thread_impl(
             };
     std::unique_ptr<pthread_attr_t, decltype(attr_deleter)> attr_scope_destroy(&attr, attr_deleter);
 
+#ifdef __VXWORKS__
+    // ThreadSettings::stack_size defaults to -1 ("use the platform default"). On Linux that pthread default
+    // is large (often 8 MiB), so -1 is harmless there. On VxWorks pthread_attr_init() selects only a 20480 byte
+    // default stack for POSIX threads, which is far too small for the discovery/receive threads and overflows
+    // (rtpSpStackSize / 'rtp exec -u' only size the RTP's initial task, not pthreads). So when the caller did
+    // not request a size (stack_size < 0), substitute a usable default instead of the 20 KiB VxWorks default.
+    if (stack_size < 0)
+    {
+        stack_size = 512 * 1024;
+    }
+#endif // ifdef __VXWORKS__
+
     // Set the requested stack size, if given.
     if (stack_size >= 0)
     {
diff --git a/thirdparty/boost/include/boost/interprocess/detail/workaround.hpp b/thirdparty/boost/include/boost/interprocess/detail/workaround.hpp
index 397d9f7..6876cbe 100644
--- a/thirdparty/boost/include/boost/interprocess/detail/workaround.hpp
+++ b/thirdparty/boost/include/boost/interprocess/detail/workaround.hpp
@@ -102,7 +102,12 @@
             defined(__APPLE__)
          #define BOOST_INTERPROCESS_POSIX_NAMED_SEMAPHORES
          //MacOsX declares _POSIX_SEMAPHORES but sem_init returns ENOSYS
-         #if !defined(__APPLE__)
+         //VxWorks declares _POSIX_SEMAPHORES but unnamed sem_init(pshared) does
+         //NOT work across RTPs: sem_t holds only a process-local SEM_ID handle,
+         //so a peer RTP's sem_post/sem_wait fail (EINVAL) even when the sem_t is
+         //in genuinely shared memory. Fall back to the spin semaphore (shared-mem
+         //atomics) which works cross-RTP. (Verified by sd_pshared_sem_probe.)
+         #if !defined(__APPLE__) && !defined(__VXWORKS__)
             #define BOOST_INTERPROCESS_POSIX_UNNAMED_SEMAPHORES
          #endif
          #if defined(__osf__) || defined(__vms)
@@ -118,7 +123,10 @@
             #define BOOST_INTERPROCESS_POSIX_NAMED_SEMAPHORES
          #endif
          //MacOsX declares _POSIX_SEMAPHORES but sem_init returns ENOSYS
-         #if !defined(__APPLE__)
+         //VxWorks: unnamed sem_init(pshared) is not cross-RTP (see above / man
+         //sem_init(2rtp): "pshared ... ignored. Unnamed semaphores cannot be
+         //accessed from other RTPs."). Use the spin fallback.
+         #if !defined(__APPLE__) && !defined(__VXWORKS__)
             #define BOOST_INTERPROCESS_POSIX_UNNAMED_SEMAPHORES
          #endif
          #if defined(__osf__) || defined(__vms)
